{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go | sed -n '1,75p' && nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go | sed -n '71,87p' && nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go | sed -n '372,418p' && nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go | sed -n '25,72p' && nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go | sed -n '1037,1055p' && nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go | sed -n '45,73p;79,116p' && nl -ba POSE.md | sed -n '1074,1080p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t//go:build linux\n     2\t\n     3\tpackage pose\n     4\t\n     5\timport (\n     6\t\t\"encoding/json\"\n     7\t\t\"errors\"\n     8\t\t\"os\"\n     9\t\t\"os/exec\"\n    10\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n    11\t\t\"strings\"\n    12\t\t\"testing\"\n    13\t\t\"time\"\n    14\t)\n    15\t\n    16\t// Spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes R5, R6: a dispatch\n    17\t// that ended between its reservation and its run record leaves an attempt\n    18\t// that blocks the bundle; once its owner is proven gone, cancel releases it\n    19\t// with a failed run and its receipt, and the ledger reads again.\n    20\tfunc TestAnAbandonedAttemptIsReleasedWithARecord(t *testing.T) {\n    21\t\troot := t.TempDir()\n    22\t\ts := Store{Root: root}\n    23\t\tbundle := \"rvb-00000000000000a1\"\n    24\t\ta := DelegatedReviewAttempt{SchemaVersion: 1, BundleID: bundle, BundleDigest: \"sha256:\" + strings.Repeat(\"a\", 64), Scope: \"spec:alpha\", Adapter: \"fake\", Ordinal: 1,\n    25\t\t\tReservedAt: time.Now().Add(-time.Hour).UTC().Format(time.RFC3339Nano), Nonce: strings.Repeat(\"0\", 32)}\n    26\t\ta.AttemptID = attemptIdentity(a)\n    27\t\trel, _ := filepath.Rel(root, reviewAttemptPath(root, a))\n    28\t\tif err := publishLedgerJSON(root, filepath.ToSlash(rel), a); err != nil {\n    29\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    30\t\t}\n    31\t\t// The ledger refuses the bundle while the reservation has no receipt.\n    32\t\tif _, err := s.readAttemptReceipt(a); err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"incomplete or unreadable\") {\n    33\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an unfinished reservation read as finished: %v\", err)\n    34\t\t}\n    35\t\n    36\t\t// The marker the interrupted dispatch left: its owner is a process that\n    37\t\t// has exited.\n    38\t\tdead := exec.Command(\"true\")\n    39\t\tif err := dead.Run(); err != nil {\n    40\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    41\t\t}\n    42\t\towner := StartLockOwner{SchemaVersion: StartLockOwnerSchemaVersion, Resource: \"delegate:\" + a.AttemptID, Worktree: root, Operation: \"pose delegate review\", PID: os.Getpid()}\n    43\t\towner.Host, _ = os.Hostname()\n    44\t\tidentifyStartLockProcess(&owner)\n    45\t\towner.PID = dead.Process.Pid\n    46\t\tmarker := DelegationActiveRun{SchemaVersion: 1, AttemptID: a.AttemptID, RunToken: strings.Repeat(\"b\", 32), Purpose: DelegationPurposeReview, Agent: \"fake\", Scope: a.Scope, BundleID: bundle,\n    47\t\t\tStartedAt: a.ReservedAt, Owner: owner, HeartbeatAt: a.ReservedAt, HeartbeatEvery: 10}\n    48\t\tdir, err := s.delegationActiveDir(true)\n    49\t\tif err != nil {\n    50\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    51\t\t}\n    52\t\traw, _ := json.Marshal(marker)\n    53\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(dir, a.AttemptID+\".json\"), raw, 0o600); err != nil {\n    54\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    55\t\t}\n    56\t\n    57\t\trun, err := s.ReleaseAbandonedAttempt(a.AttemptID, time.Now())\n    58\t\tif err != nil {\n    59\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    60\t\t}\n    61\t\tif run.Status != ReviewRunFailed || !strings.Contains(run.Failure, \"abandoned\") {\n    62\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the release recorded %s: %s\", run.Status, run.Failure)\n    63\t\t}\n    64\t\tif _, err := s.readAttemptReceipt(a); err != nil {\n    65\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the released attempt still blocks the bundle: %v\", err)\n    66\t\t}\n    67\t\tif left, _ := filepath.Glob(filepath.Join(dir, a.AttemptID+\"*\")); len(left) != 0 {\n    68\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the marker or its stall claim stayed: %v\", left)\n    69\t\t}\n    70\t\t// Released once: a second release finds nothing abandoned.\n    71\t\tif _, err := s.ReleaseAbandonedAttempt(a.AttemptID, time.Now()); !errors.Is(err, ErrAttemptNotAbandoned) {\n    72\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a released attempt was released again: %v\", err)\n    73\t\t}\n    74\t}\n    75\t\n    71\t// ListDelegationAttempts groups every recorded run by attempt, adds the runs\n    72\t// in progress, and returns the losses the run history reports.\n    73\tfunc (s Store) ListDelegationAttempts() ([]DelegationAttempt, []string, error) {\n    74\t\t// The markers are read before the runs: a run publishes its record before\n    75\t\t// it removes its marker, so a reader that finds no marker for an attempt\n    76\t\t// it saw running finds its record (spec\n    77\t\t// pose-delegated-review-completion-signal R5).\n    78\t\tactive, activeLost, activeErr := s.ListDelegationActive()\n    79\t\truns, lost, err := s.ReadReviewRuns(\"\")\n    80\t\tif err != nil {\n    81\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n    82\t\t}\n    83\t\t// Task runs share the lifecycle, never the review history (spec\n    84\t\t// pose-delegation-task R7, R8).\n    85\t\ttasks, taskLost := s.ReadDelegationTaskRuns()\n    86\t\truns, lost = append(runs, tasks...), append(lost, taskLost...)\n    87\t\tbyAttempt := map[string]*DelegationAttempt{}\n   372\tfunc (s Store) reviewAttemptAdmission(plan DispatchPlan) ([]DelegatedReviewAttempt, int, error) {\n   373\t\tif len(plan.Reason) > 2048 || strings.ContainsAny(plan.Reason, \"\\x00\\r\\n\") {\n   374\t\t\treturn nil, 0, fmt.Errorf(\"rerun reason must be one line of at most 2048 bytes\")\n   375\t\t}\n   376\t\truns, lost, err := s.ReadReviewRuns(plan.Bundle.BundleID)\n   377\t\tif err != nil {\n   378\t\t\treturn nil, 0, err\n   379\t\t}\n   380\t\tif len(lost) > 0 {\n   381\t\t\treturn nil, 0, fmt.Errorf(\"review run coverage is unknown: %v\", lost)\n   382\t\t}\n   383\t\tattempts, err := s.readDelegatedReviewAttempts(plan.Bundle.BundleID)\n   384\t\tif err != nil {\n   385\t\t\treturn nil, 0, err\n   386\t\t}\n   387\t\tknownAttempts := map[string]bool{}\n   388\t\tcount := 0\n   389\t\treceiptBudget := int64(32 << 20)\n   390\t\tfor _, a := range attempts {\n   391\t\t\tknownAttempts[a.AttemptID] = true\n   392\t\t\tif _, err := s.readAttemptReceipt(a, &receiptBudget); err != nil {\n   393\t\t\t\treturn nil, 0, err\n   394\t\t\t}\n   395\t\t\tif a.Adapter == plan.Adapter {\n   396\t\t\t\tcount++\n   397\t\t\t}\n   398\t\t}\n   399\t\tcompleted := false\n   400\t\tfor _, run := range runs {\n   401\t\t\tif run.AttemptID != \"\" && !knownAttempts[run.AttemptID] {\n   402\t\t\t\treturn nil, 0, fmt.Errorf(\"missing attempt reservation %s\", run.AttemptID)\n   403\t\t\t}\n   404\t\t\tif run.Status == ReviewRunCompleted {\n   405\t\t\t\tcompleted = true\n   406\t\t\t}\n   407\t\t\tif run.AttemptID == \"\" && run.Adapter == plan.Adapter {\n   408\t\t\t\tcount++\n   409\t\t\t}\n   410\t\t}\n   411\t\tif count >= effectiveReviewMaxRuns(plan.Config) {\n   412\t\t\treturn nil, count, refusal(DelegationReasonBudgetExhausted, fmt.Errorf(\"budget exhausted: %d attempt(s) of %s on this bundle, at most %d\", count, plan.Adapter, effectiveReviewMaxRuns(plan.Config)))\n   413\t\t}\n   414\t\tif completed && strings.TrimSpace(plan.Reason) == \"\" {\n   415\t\t\treturn nil, count, refusal(DelegationReasonRerunWithoutReason, fmt.Errorf(\"completed run exists on unchanged bundle; an explicit --reason is required\"))\n   416\t\t}\n   417\t\treturn attempts, count, nil\n   418\t}\n    25\t// ReleaseAbandonedAttempt records the failed run of an attempt whose\n    26\t// dispatch ended before recording it, and removes its stalled marker.\n    27\tfunc (s Store) ReleaseAbandonedAttempt(attemptID string, now time.Time) (ReviewRun, error) {\n    28\t\tmarkers, _, err := s.ListDelegationActive()\n    29\t\tif err != nil {\n    30\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n    31\t\t}\n    32\t\tvar marker *DelegationActiveRun\n    33\t\tfor i := range markers {\n    34\t\t\tif markers[i].AttemptID == attemptID {\n    35\t\t\t\tmarker = &markers[i]\n    36\t\t\t}\n    37\t\t}\n    38\t\tif marker == nil || marker.StalledAt == \"\" || marker.Liveness != LockOwnerDead {\n    39\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: its owner is not proven gone\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned)\n    40\t\t}\n    41\t\tattempts, err := s.readDelegatedReviewAttempts(marker.BundleID)\n    42\t\tif err != nil {\n    43\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n    44\t\t}\n    45\t\tvar reserved *DelegatedReviewAttempt\n    46\t\tfor i := range attempts {\n    47\t\t\tif attempts[i].AttemptID == attemptID {\n    48\t\t\t\treserved = &attempts[i]\n    49\t\t\t}\n    50\t\t}\n    51\t\tif reserved == nil {\n    52\t\t\t// The dispatch ended between its marker and its reservation: nothing\n    53\t\t\t// blocks the bundle, and the marker alone is removed.\n    54\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, s.removeDelegationMarker(*marker)\n    55\t\t}\n    56\t\tif _, err := os.Lstat(attemptReceiptPath(s.Root, *reserved)); !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n    57\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: it already has a receipt\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned)\n    58\t\t}\n    59\t\trun := ReviewRun{SchemaVersion: 1, Scope: reserved.Scope, BundleID: reserved.BundleID, BundleDigest: reserved.BundleDigest,\n    60\t\t\tKind: DelegationKindForPurpose(marker.Purpose), Adapter: reserved.Adapter, Reason: reserved.Reason, AttemptID: reserved.AttemptID,\n    61\t\t\tStartedAt: marker.StartedAt, ExitCode: -1, Label: marker.Label, Purpose: marker.Purpose, Round: marker.Round,\n    62\t\t\tStatus: ReviewRunFailed, Failure: DelegationAbandonedCause + \" (stalled at \" + marker.StalledAt + \"); released by pose delegate cancel\",\n    63\t\t\tEndedAt: now.UTC().Format(time.RFC3339Nano)}\n    64\t\trecorded, err := s.recordReviewRun(run, nil)\n    65\t\tif err != nil {\n    66\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n    67\t\t}\n    68\t\tif err := s.finishDelegatedReviewAttempt(*reserved, recorded); err != nil {\n    69\t\t\treturn recorded, err\n    70\t\t}\n    71\t\treturn recorded, s.removeDelegationMarker(*marker)\n    72\t}\n  1037\t\tterminationErr = killProcessGroup(cmd)\n  1038\t\t// A command the reviewer left running in a session of its own escapes the\n  1039\t\t// group kill; it is ended here, before the cleanup inventory reads the\n  1040\t\t// directories it may still write (spec\n  1041\t\t// pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes R1, R2).\n  1042\t\treaped, opaque, reapErr := reapSealedCheckoutProcesses(worktree)\n  1043\t\tif reapErr != nil {\n  1044\t\t\tterminationErr = errors.Join(terminationErr, reapErr)\n  1045\t\t}\n  1046\t\tif len(reaped) > 0 && safety != nil {\n  1047\t\t\tsafety.Limitations = append(safety.Limitations, \"ended \"+fmt.Sprint(len(reaped))+\" process(es) the run left running: \"+strings.Join(reaped, \", \"))\n  1048\t\t}\n  1049\t\tif opaque > 0 && safety != nil {\n  1050\t\t\tsafety.Limitations = append(safety.Limitations, fmt.Sprint(opaque)+\" process(es) of this user could not be inspected for the run's environment entry; any of them the run started was not ended\")\n  1051\t\t}\n  1052\t\tterminationFailed = terminationErr != nil\n  1053\t\t// The adapter exited and a child it left still held the output when\n  1054\t\t// WaitDelay expired: the run finished, its leftover is killed above, and\n  1055\t\t// the exit status decides (found in review).\n    45\t\t}\n    46\t\tentry := []byte(SealedCheckoutEnv + \"=\" + worktree)\n    47\t\tvar reaped []string\n    48\t\tseen := map[int]bool{}\n    49\t\tdeadline := time.Now().Add(reviewReapWait)\n    50\t\tunreadable := 0\n    51\t\tfor {\n    52\t\t\talive, opaque, err := reviewMarkedProcesses(entry)\n    53\t\t\tif err != nil {\n    54\t\t\t\treturn reaped, opaque, err\n    55\t\t\t}\n    56\t\t\tunreadable = opaque\n    57\t\t\tfor _, pid := range alive {\n    58\t\t\t\tif !seen[pid] {\n    59\t\t\t\t\tseen[pid] = true\n    60\t\t\t\t\treaped = append(reaped, fmt.Sprintf(\"%d %s\", pid, reviewProcessName(pid)))\n    61\t\t\t\t}\n    62\t\t\t\tif err := killPinnedMarkedProcess(pid, entry); err != nil {\n    63\t\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, err\n    64\t\t\t\t}\n    65\t\t\t}\n    66\t\t\tif len(alive) == 0 {\n    67\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, nil\n    68\t\t\t}\n    69\t\t\tif time.Now().After(deadline) {\n    70\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"%d process(es) of the run could not be ended\", len(alive))\n    71\t\t\t}\n    72\t\t\ttime.Sleep(50 * time.Millisecond)\n    73\t\t}\n    79\tfunc reviewMarkedProcesses(entry []byte) ([]int, int, error) {\n    80\t\tdirs, err := os.ReadDir(\"/proc\")\n    81\t\tif err != nil {\n    82\t\t\treturn nil, 0, fmt.Errorf(\"the run's processes could not be listed: %w\", err)\n    83\t\t}\n    84\t\tunreadable := 0\n    85\t\tself, uid := os.Getpid(), os.Getuid()\n    86\t\tvar out []int\n    87\t\tfor _, d := range dirs {\n    88\t\t\tpid, err := strconv.Atoi(d.Name())\n    89\t\t\tif err != nil || pid == self {\n    90\t\t\t\tcontinue\n    91\t\t\t}\n    92\t\t\tmarked, err := reviewProcessMarked(pid, entry)\n    93\t\t\tswitch {\n    94\t\t\tcase reviewProcessGoneErr(err):\n    95\t\t\t\tcontinue\n    96\t\t\tcase err != nil:\n    97\t\t\t\tif owner, oerr := reviewProcessOwner(pid); oerr == nil && owner != uid {\n    98\t\t\t\t\tcontinue // another user's process never inherits this run's environment\n    99\t\t\t\t} else if reviewProcessGoneErr(oerr) {\n   100\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   101\t\t\t\t}\n   102\t\t\t\tunreadable++\n   103\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   104\t\t\tcase !marked:\n   105\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   106\t\t\t}\n   107\t\t\tzombie, err := reviewProcessZombie(pid)\n   108\t\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(err) || err == nil && zombie {\n   109\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   110\t\t\t}\n   111\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   112\t\t\t\treturn nil, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d state could not be read: %w\", pid, err)\n   113\t\t\t}\n   114\t\t\tout = append(out, pid)\n   115\t\t}\n   116\t\treturn out, unreadable, nil\n  1074\t**Conclusions of delegated reviews.** `pose review conclude <run> [--issuer <name>] [--apply] [--json]` records the conclusion of a completed review run: the run's final message carries its typed conclusion in the pose-draft block — `criteria` (`id`, `disposition` passed|finding|not-applicable, `evidence` as `<class>:<ref>`, `rationale`, and `mappings` where the plan asks for structural mappings) and `tools` (`id`, `component`, `disposition`, `evidence`, `rationale`), the brief of template `review-brief/10` (the text a template version renders is frozen by a golden digest, so a change to it takes a new version) asks for them and states the rules the engine checks before it records one (a judgment criterion passed carries a rationale, its evidence is a ref the bundle sealed, a finding criterion names a finding of the draft, structural facts are answered as `mappings`; a draft that breaks one is refused whole; a round after the first also names the findings it accounts for by the identifiers the brief lists, with their round, never a bare F1) — and the engine signs the run's proof and the attestation with the native issuer, `--issuer` or `conclusions.issuer` in `.pose/policy/delegation.json` (the key stays outside the project), and records it through the same domain writer and preflight as `pose review attest --run --run-proof --sign`. A follow-up finding with `action`, `owner` and `review_by` becomes an accepted risk when its severity is one the sealed review policy accepts (low by default); any other finding stays open. A rejecting conclusion is recorded too and blocks the scope until the bundle changes. A run that is not a completed review, is superseded, captured no provenance, has an incomplete cleanup or record, carries no valid draft for its round, or whose bundle no longer governs, records no attestation: its conclusion record, in the `review-conclusions` directory of `.pose`, keeps the reasons. A run concludes once: a lock the system releases when the process ends is held from the first read to the last write, concluding it again returns its record, and a reservation an interrupted conclusion left is completed from the attestation it recorded only if that attestation verifies as the run's conclusion, otherwise the run is concluded in its place. Whoever signs it, an attestation of a run briefed with `review-brief/3` to `/10` states that run's conclusion: criteria, tools or findings its draft did not declare are refused. With review policy `delegated_review: true` and `conclusions.issuer` set, `pose delegate review` records the conclusion the moment the run completes; otherwise nothing is automatic. An adjudication or a smoke run concludes the same way, under the same checks, lock and refusals, and never as an approval. The brief of template `adjudication-brief/2` lists the questions the scope's spec records — each decision `D<n>` and requirement `R<n>` — and the pose-draft block answers each in `questions` (`id`, `verdict` holds|does-not-hold|cannot-determine, `evidence`, `rationale`); the verdict is recorded as an adjudication record of the spec in the `adjudications` directory of `.pose`, and `lint-spec` fails, and `close` refuses, on a question the current bundle's adjudication says does not hold and warns on one it cannot determine or on a record that does not verify. The brief of template `smoke-brief/2` asks for `surfaces` (`ref`, `outcome` observed|not-observed|not-reachable, `commands`, `observed`), one per delivery target; the observations are recorded as validation results of evidence class `smoke`, one required check per target that passes when it was observed and is evidence of that target of that spec only, its head, time and provenance taken from the run and the current index, in the `results/smoke` directory of `.pose`, which `surface-check` reads beside the results path, so a delivery profile may demand `smoke`. A verdict that does not answer exactly what its brief asked records nothing; every record is verified on read — its run's proof verifies and it is what the run's draft concludes — and one that does not yields nothing. Runs briefed with `adjudication-brief/1` and `smoke-brief/1` keep verifying with their template.\n  1075\t\n  1076\t**Review readiness before the seal.** A new seal of a spec scope refuses what `pose close` and the conclusion preflight would otherwise refuse only after a full review round: a change to a delivery root with no delivery declaration (`undeclared-delivery`) or to a governed path the artifacts do not declare (`undeclared`), read from the same index `pose close` reads, and, when a required criterion asks for structural mappings, a decision or assumption that reaches no requirement or constraint (give it a `- Basis:` line). A bundle already sealed is returned as it was. `pose review draft-check [<bundle-id|run-id>] --draft <file|-> [--json]` reports every reason the conclusion step would refuse a draft (an unreadable block, a round it does not account for, a criterion, mapping, finding, evidence or tool the attestation preflight refuses) and writes nothing; inside a delegated review the run provides the bundle and the round through `POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT_CONTEXT` and names its own engine in `POSE_REVIEW_CLI`, and `-` reads the draft from standard input, so it works in a read-only sandbox. The brief of template `review-brief/8` asks the reviewer to run it before finishing; `review-brief/9` also has every planned `pose` command run as `\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\"`, because the `pose` the reviewer's shell resolves may be an older engine. `pose delegate` names an oversized note file with its size and the limit, and a completed run that nothing concluded automatically prints the `pose review conclude <run>` command that records it.\n  1077\t\n  1078\t**Runs that leave work behind.** On Linux, after the adapter exits, the dispatch also ends every process whose environment names the run's sealed checkout (`POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT`), which catches commands a reviewer started in a session of its own; each is pinned by a pidfd and checked again before it is signalled. It waits for them and lists them in the run's `safety.limitations` before the cleanup inventory, and discloses there any process of the same user whose environment could not be read; on other platforms only the process group is ended; the brief of template `review-brief/10` asks the reviewer to let its commands finish. The dispatch marks an attempt active before it publishes its reservation, so a dispatch that ends before recording its run always leaves a stalled attempt, which `pose delegate ls` lists with its cause; `pose delegate cancel <attempt>` releases it once its owner is proven gone, recording a failed run and its receipt.\n  1079\t\n  1080\t**Delegated-review requests.** `pose review request <scope|bundle> --kind delegated-review [--purpose review|adjudicate|smoke] [--agents <name,...>] [--note-file <path>] [--apply]` opens an action request of kind `delegated-review` that binds the project, the worktree, the scope, the sealed bundle, the brief, the notes, the policies, the accepted agents and the destination of the conclusion (an attestation, an adjudication record or smoke evidence). No actor answers it: `pose action fulfil <act-id> --run <run-id> --runner agent:<id> --idempotency-key <key> --expected-revision <n> [--channel cli|ci|conductor] [--envelope <file>] [--apply]`, or the MCP tool `pose_action_fulfil`, submits a completed run, and the engine records the fulfilment only when the run is of the request's brief and bundle, of an accepted agent, completed with its containment, its signed proof verifies, its attempt ledger is intact and the engine recorded its conclusion at the request's destination; the fulfilment is verified again on every read. `pose delegate review <scope> --request <act-id>` runs the request's brief locally and submits the run once concluded. A rejecting run fulfils the request without approving anything; a superseded bundle or changed policy invalidates it, even once fulfilled, and it is asked again with `--supersedes <act-id>`, which retires it under the supersession authority rules (`--authority <json>`, `--role <role>`, `--requested-at` from the preview), or, when the plan now reserves the review for a person, makes the person's escalation its successor; a retry with the same key and run is a no-op. A person is asked by exception, as a decision request to the maintainer role: a plan that reserves the review for a person, a spent attempt budget, reviewers in conflict, and a `business_decision` a reviewer raised in its draft. A run's proof verifies in any checkout of the project: the worktree it ran in is recorded, not required of the reader, so a CI job or the Conductor fulfils the request with the same envelope.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
